WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.160
Some weeks ago, we ran an episode about the
Vatican City State in our sister channel,

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.160
Geographics.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:33.110
In that video, I mentioned one of the tiny
state’s most peculiar residents, and many

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:36.800
of you asked me to expand on his life here
at Biographics.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:43.210
I am talking about Father Gabriele Amorth,
the most experienced and prolific exorcist

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.940
in force at the Vatican.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:51.100
Between the start of his career in 1986, until
shortly before his death in 2016, Father Amorth

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.510
claimed to have exorcised 300 subjects per
year.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.900
Let’s get into it then!

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:02.210
How did Gabriele Amorth become a priest, and
more importantly, an exorcist?

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.930
Fighter, Student, Priest.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:13.710
Gabriele Amorth was born on May 1, 1925 in
Modena, Northern Italy, now famous for being

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.030
the home of Ferrari.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:21.490
Modena also had a high concentration of alleged
witches and wizards, especially from the 15th

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:22.799
through the 18th Centuries.

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:28.030
Some of them were just experts in herbal remedies,
but they still had to face the local Inquisition,

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:30.909
active from the 13th to the 18th Century.

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:35.590
One of these occult individuals deserves a
special mention: Father Guglielmo Campana.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:42.450
A renowned local priest, Campana was an exorcist,
but also a womanizer, a sorcerer, and a necromancer.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.570
He was duly tried by the Inquisition in 1517.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:49.969
We don’t know if young Gabriele was aware
of these stories.

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:55.009
What we do know is that he grew up in a household
that was both religious and involved in politics:

00:01:55.009 --> 00:02:00.159
his father was an early supporter of the People’s
Party, a faction inspired by Catholic ideals

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:04.069
and the precursor to the eventual Christian
Democrat Party.

00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:09.880
In 1943, Gabriele turned 18 and was drafted
into the Fascist army, but he went AWOL and

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.400
joined a resistance unit headed by a Catholic
activist.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:18.210
For the following two years, Amorth fought
against Fascist loyalists and German occupation

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:21.569
forces, rising to the rank of Battalion Commander
within the resistance.

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:24.569
That’s equivalent to an Army Major.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:26.510
All at the age of 20!

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:29.959
It’s reassuring to know that your local
demon hunter was also handy with a Carcano

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:32.340
rifle and a STEN sub-machine gun!

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.510
Amorth reported being arrested and sentenced
to death more than once, but he always managed

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.510
to escape.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:41.010
After the end of the war, Amorth was awarded
the War Cross for Military Valour.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.739
After returning to civilian life, Gabriele
moved to Rome to study law.

00:02:44.739 --> 00:02:50.430
He also became active in politics: in 1947,
he joined the recently founded Christian Democrats

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.959
as vice secretary of the Party’s youth organisation.

00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:58.689
The secretary in charge was one Giulio Andreotti,
a controversial figure who later became a

00:02:58.689 --> 00:03:01.180
cabinet Minister and eventually Prime Minister.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.420
But Gabriele didn’t pursue politics.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.470
Since the age of 17, Amorth had considered
joining the Church and so, after earning his

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:12.269
law degree, he enrolled in a seminary to become
a man of the cloth.

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:17.159
In 1954, Gabriele attained a second degree
in theology, and was ordained as a Catholic

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:19.370
priest.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:25.630
Black Dog
During his first years in priesthood, Father

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:30.239
Amorth did not practice exorcisms, nor was
he probably even aware of these rituals.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:34.959
At that time, the number of exorcist priests
in Italy could be counted on two hands.

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:40.050
However, Amorth did dedicate himself to some
of the most miraculous, supernatural and even

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.760
controversial aspects of the faith.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:46.970
A long devotee of the Virgin Mary, Amorth
studied the Marian apparitions and miracles

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.300
at Medjugorje, in modern-day Bosnia.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:53.099
He firmly believed these to be true-life events,
a point of fact not endorsed or agreed upon

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:54.670
by all the clergy members.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:59.190
In 1959, he visited another site famous for
miracles attributed to the Mother of Jesus:

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.750
Fatima, in Portugal.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.440
In a spectacular enterprise, Father Amorth
organised a ‘pilgrimage in reverse’ -- he

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.659
arranged for a statue of the Virgin to travel
from Fatima to all of Italy’s main cities.

00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:15.930
His old pal Andreotti, now Minister of Defence,
assisted by loaning Amorth some military transport

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.220
helicopters!

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.900
During this tour Father Amorth took the statue
to the Convent of Padre Pio, or Father Pius,

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:23.900
now a Saint.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.900
[Note: ‘Pio’ is pronounced ‘Pea-aw’,
not ‘Pie-aw’]

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.800
This mystic friar is widely believed to have
performed miracles during his lifetime and

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:29.930
after his death.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:35.270
He was also beset with stigmata: unexplained
bleeding marks which appear on the ribs, wrists,

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:39.320
hands or feet, matching the wounds that Jesus
Christs received on the cross.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:44.260
It was Father Pio who first introduced Father
Amorth to the mysteries of the Devil and its

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.780
presence among humans.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:50.350
Often the Prince of Darkness would torment
Pio, disguised as a huge, snarling black dog.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.720
While the friar prayed alone in his convent
cell, the hell hound would attack him, forcing

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.310
him into vicious, all-night-long fights.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:02.780
Father Pio died in 1968 and was canonised
as a Saint in June 2002.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.600
During the ensuing years, Father Amorth did
not have direct contact with any demons.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:11.250
The closest he got was was his acquaintance
with Father Candido Amantini, who for much

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:16.180
of the 1960s, ‘70s and ‘80s, was the only
sanctioned exorcist in Rome.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.200
But things were about to change.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:23.020
In 1986, Father Amorth was 61 -- an age close
to retirement for most people!

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:27.320
And yet, his true career was just about to
start.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:33.660
On June 6, 1986, Father Amorth was summoned
for a meeting with Cardinal Poletti, the highest-ranking

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.380
clergyman in Rome, besides the Pope.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:41.740
During a casual conversation, Poletti asked
if Amorth knew Father Amantini, the exorcist.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:46.130
As Amorth answered that yes, he had met him
previously, he noticed that Poletti was scribbling

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.130
on a piece of paper.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.480
At the end of the conversation, the Cardinal
handed him a note -- it was an official appointment

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:53.080
as assistant to Amantini.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:58.380
Just like that, Amorth had become assistant
exorcist for Rome, which essentially made

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.820
him the deputy-chief exorcist of the Vatican.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:04.750
He understood immediately that he was going
to become more than an assistant -- he would

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:10.470
soon become Amantini’s successor, as the
current chief exorcist was in poor health.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:14.190
Amantini held on for another six years, dying
in September 1992.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:20.460
From 1986 to 1992, Amorth learned from his
mentor all the tricks of that terrifying trade

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.940
that is the casting away of demons.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:28.650
I will now ask you to step into Gabriele’s
shoes, as I take the role of Amantini and

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:33.180
take you through a quick apprenticeship on
how to become a Demon Slayer.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.930
First lesson: what is possession?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:43.890
By Demons Be Driven
According to the official Catholic Catechism,

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:49.240
demonic possession is the act by which the
Devil, a demon, or a spirit takes over a victim’s

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.830
physical activity, as well as their mental
and spiritual energies.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:57.390
By exerting physical violence upon the hosts,
which manifests for the victim as illness

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:01.930
or pain, the demons can coerce humans into
committing unholy sins.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:04.630
What exactly is the ultimate goal of these
malignant entities?

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:08.210
In most cases, it’s just to spread chaos
for the sheer pleasure of it.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:12.900
The possession cases that Amantini and Amorth
involved themselves in mainly belonged to

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.640
a category defined as ‘peripheral pathogenic’
by modern anthropology.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:22.290
Anthropologist I.M. Lewis makes a distinction
between central and peripheral types of possession.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.290
[Editing note: Show a graphic on screen, two
text boxes would be sufficient to illustrate

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.851
the two categories of Central and Peripheral]
In the case of Central Possession, a member

00:07:24.851 --> 00:07:29.310
of the religious elite becomes possessed by
spirits during an official ceremony in which

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:33.390
he or she fulfils a political, religious,
or moral function.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:38.590
Peripheral possession, on the other hand,
indicates an invasion of evil spirits: unwanted,

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.400
immoral, dangerous.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:44.440
Anthropologist Emma Cohen further subclassifies
peripheral possession into ‘executive’

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.440
and ‘pathogenic’.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.160
[Editing note: The Peripheral box splits into
the two subgroups, Executive and Pathogenic]

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.810
Executive possessions involve the complete
replacement or transformation of the host’s

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:54.300
personality with that of the invading entity.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:59.590
In pathogenic cases, the spirit or demon will
cause abnormal and deviant behaviour, illness,

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:03.490
pain or misfortune to the victims, while their
identity is largely intact.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:07.910
It’s the alternating of normal and abnormal
behaviour that leads the victims’ social

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.760
circle to seek help.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:13.990
The world’s largest religions all have their
interpretations of what entities may cause

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:16.780
these peripheral pathogenic possessions.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:22.000
According to the Talmud, a sacred book of
Jewish tradition, possession is called Dybbuk:

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.602
this is when the soul of a dead person is
‘grafted’ onto a living person’s soul.

00:08:25.602 --> 00:08:26.680
This may happen out of revenge, sheer malice,
or total randomness.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:31.030
In Islam, those who are greedy for earthly
pleasures, have low self-esteem, or struggle

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:34.130
for acceptance may be possessed by a Jinn.

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:38.770
According to the Quran, these are entities
made of smokeless, scorching fire and are

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.490
not necessarily malevolent.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:45.399
In Hindu lore, unwelcome possessions manifest
as physical or mental illnesses, mainly affecting

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:46.460
women and children.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:51.149
These are caused by a number of evil forces,
such as bhutas, or ghosts, curails, blood-sucking

00:08:51.149 --> 00:08:55.839
witches, pisacas, flesh-eating demons, and
many more.

00:08:55.839 --> 00:09:00.870
Going back to Catholicism, the Catechism identifies
possessing entities a either the Devil himself

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.220
or, much more commonly, his demons.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:07.000
These are fallen angels, which means that
their strength, intellect, knowledge, and

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.449
cunning are superior to that of humans.

00:09:09.449 --> 00:09:14.120
Nonetheless, they are still God’s creatures
and are ultimately subject to His will.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:17.629
That is why an ordained member of the Church
can perform exorcisms.

00:09:17.629 --> 00:09:22.259
These are simply defined as acts or rites
by which priests use their authority to demand

00:09:22.259 --> 00:09:26.240
that a person – or even an object - is rid
of the influence of Evil.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:31.339
Father Amantini introduced his pupil Gabriele
to the strictly codified procedures to conduct

00:09:31.339 --> 00:09:35.439
an exorcism, as defined by Ecclesiastical
Law and the Roman Ritual.

00:09:35.439 --> 00:09:40.260
This is the official collection of sacred
rites and prayers to be used during the Sacraments.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:45.399
But before you can start to exorcise a patient,
how can you be sure that a demon is lurking

00:09:45.399 --> 00:10:18.649
within?

00:10:18.649 --> 00:11:33.310
Scorpions and Serpents
Amorth learned how to approach every potential

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:36.540
case of possession with a process called nment.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:40.120
First, patients must present with clear symptoms.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:43.660
Besides irrational changes in one’s behaviour,
including performing acts of violence and

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:48.080
self-harm, there are some physical symptoms:
the white of the eyes may appear red, as in

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:49.329
a case of conjunctivitis.

00:11:49.329 --> 00:11:52.720
The pupil will be excessively and constantly
dilated.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.860
The patient’s face will appear longer and
darker than normal.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:12:01.040
So far, all of these symptoms are compatible
with known physical and psychiatric ailments.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.519
But others stand out much more clearly.

00:12:03.519 --> 00:12:07.240
Some patients would display immense, inexplicable
physical strength.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.959
Their voice may become unnaturally hoarse
and deep.

00:12:09.959 --> 00:12:14.120
They will speak, or understand, languages
previously unknown to them, such as Latin,

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.779
Ancient Greek, or Aramaic.

00:12:15.779 --> 00:12:20.240
They will react violently to the presence
of sacred objects or the mention of religious

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:21.240
figures.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:25.759
In extreme cases, just thinking about Jesus
or Mary may throw patients into a fit of rage.

00:12:25.759 --> 00:12:27.300
If patients carried these symptoms,
[Editing note: let’s add some captions specifying

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.300
the steps of the Ritual, so it is clearer
for viewers.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.300
The caption here is: Step 1 – Identification
of symptoms of possession]

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:31.590
Amorth and Amantini would organise a prayer
service with them, also known as a ‘diagnostic

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:32.590
exorcism’.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:35.319
[Caption: Step 2 – Diagnostic Exorcism]
If patients were to react adversely, suggesting

00:12:35.319 --> 00:12:39.260
an actual possession, the exorcists would
refer them to a medical team for further evaluation.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.290
[Caption: Step 3 – Medical Referral and
Evaluation]

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:44.899
This is a very important step, as Father Amorth
– and all exorcists in general – recognized

00:12:44.899 --> 00:12:47.730
the importance of proper psychiatric evaluation.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:51.139
If no medical explanation or remedy were found
for the victim's suffering, the priest would

00:12:51.139 --> 00:12:55.290
then decide whether to proceed with the exorcism
and seek permission from his local Bishop.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.290
[Caption: Step 4 – Authorisation from Local
Bishop]

00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:00.149
By shadowing Amantini, Father Amorth perfected
his exorcism rites.

00:13:00.149 --> 00:13:04.680
According to the Roman Ritual, these must
be conducted by a priest, in Latin or another

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.540
Vatican-approved language, while standing
on sacred ground,.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:10.430
[Caption: Step 5 – The Exorcism Begins]
The Roman Ritual is rigidly codified: priests

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:15.740
are meant to follow a pre-ordained sequence
of prayers, psalms, and exhortations intended

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:18.230
to expel demons from the hosts’ body.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:22.529
Amorth largely followed the Ritual during
his apprenticeship, but he eventually introduced

00:13:22.529 --> 00:13:24.249
some personal touches.

00:13:24.249 --> 00:13:29.220
For example, he always wore a purple stole,
which he ensured was wrapped around both his

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:30.600
and his patients’ shoulders.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:35.370
He always made sure he was carrying Holy Water
and a bearing a medal of Saint Benedict of

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.370
Nursia.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:39.779
This Saint is mostly known for his lasting
influence on monastic life and education,

00:13:39.779 --> 00:13:43.360
but he is also famous for defeating Satan
on at least three occasions.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:48.149
Over time, Amorth realised that more than
90 percent of his cases that made it to Step

00:13:48.149 --> 00:13:50.800
5 turned out not to be real possessions.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:55.150
That is why he developed a further screening
method, which worked only once an exorcism

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.150
was under way.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:14:00.339
Amorth claimed that during the ritual, many
patients would close their eyes during specific

00:14:00.339 --> 00:14:01.339
prayers.

00:14:01.339 --> 00:14:03.959
In turn, Amorth would have their eyelids forced
open.

00:14:03.959 --> 00:14:08.139
In the case of real possessions, the eyes
appeared completely white.

00:14:08.139 --> 00:14:13.510
In an interview with British broadcaster Giles
Brandreth, Amorth specified that if the pupils

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:17.300
are completely rolled upwards,
“ … then the demons in possession are

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:18.300
scorpions.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:22.829
If looking down, they are serpents”
Amorth did not elaborate on this distinction.

00:14:22.829 --> 00:14:28.589
But serpents, or snakes, are a common incarnation
of Satan or his demons in Christian art and

00:14:28.589 --> 00:14:29.709
literature.

00:14:29.709 --> 00:14:33.380
Scorpion demons are more interesting, though,
as they belong to the Mesopotamian mythology

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:36.870
that pre-dates any description of Judeo-Christian
demons.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:43.649
It was a Mesopotamian demon, Pazuzu, that
appeared as the main antagonist in The Exorcist.

00:14:43.649 --> 00:14:47.879
After a period in which Father Amorth closely
shadowed his mentor, he finally had the chance

00:14:47.879 --> 00:14:50.920
to perform his first exorcism as the lead.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:56.050
This case related to a 14-year-old girl, who
after attending a Satanic ritual in central

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:58.829
Rome, immediately presented with symptoms
of possession.

00:14:58.829 --> 00:15:04.709
Her parents took her immediately to Amantini,
but unfortunately the lead exorcist was ill.

00:15:04.709 --> 00:15:05.769
Amorth stepped forward.

00:15:05.769 --> 00:15:11.360
In a rare instance of disobedience, he disregarded
the discernment process and immediately started

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.360
the ritual.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:15.630
In later interviews, he claimed that the girl
was healed after one single session.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:20.070
He explained this by citing the immediacy
of the exorcism, which had prevented the demon

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:24.490
or spirit from
“Taking root, or burrowing, inside the victim.”

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:29.809
This was an exception: in most cases, patients
were taken to Amantini and Amorth only after

00:15:29.809 --> 00:15:32.569
months of suffering from possession symptoms.

00:15:32.569 --> 00:15:37.529
According to Amorth’s new theory, this enabled
invading spirits to settle inside the hosts.

00:15:37.529 --> 00:15:42.570
This demonic fortification required exorcisms
to continue for multiple sittings, at least

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:48.249
an hour long, over the span of months or even
years, until a patient was eventually liberated.

00:15:48.249 --> 00:15:49.860
Is liberation a given?

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:54.670
Father Amorth became increasingly confident
about his odds of victory with each passing

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:55.670
exorcism.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:59.819
The teaching of Amantini was that, regardless
of their power, demons will ultimately succumb

00:15:59.819 --> 00:16:03.129
to the power of Christ, if properly channelled
through an exorcist.

00:16:03.129 --> 00:16:06.810
Father Amorth once told a journalist that
“The Devil may win some battles.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:08.129
Even important ones.

00:16:08.129 --> 00:16:11.999
But remember:
He will never win the war”

00:16:11.999 --> 00:16:19.910
A Duel with Satan
Father Amorth indeed waged a constant war

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.649
against the legions of Hell.

00:16:21.649 --> 00:16:26.550
Since his appointment in 1986, until his death
in 2016, the chief exorcist dealt with more

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:29.050
than 300 cases of possession every year.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:35.160
That’s a rough total of 10,000 alleged possessions,
requiring him to perform about 70,000 exorcism

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.160
sessions.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:40.499
However, Father Amorth always admitted that
the actual cases of demonic possession were

00:16:40.499 --> 00:16:42.949
in the hundreds, not the thousands.

00:16:42.949 --> 00:16:47.569
In most cases, exorcism didn’t work; patients
were referred back to psychiatric care and

00:16:47.569 --> 00:16:49.230
eventually cured by other means.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:53.189
In actual cases of possession, Father Amorth
estimated that 90 percent of them were due

00:16:53.189 --> 00:16:57.269
to the patient’s exposure to a spell, a
curse, or a satanic ritual.

00:16:57.269 --> 00:17:02.120
Amorth acknowledges that most self-described
witches, wizards, clairvoyants, or Satanist

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:07.800
priests are harmless occult enthusiasts at
best, or mundane scammers at worst.

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:12.650
However, he believes that a small minority
of them have actual dark powers.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:17.610
What are the effects of confirmed possession
on its victims?

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:21.610
Let’s take the example of one of Amorth’s
youngest patients, a boy of 11.

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:25.240
Halfway through the ritual, the boy – or
the demon within – flew into such a fit

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:29.870
of rage that he had to be restrained by seven
grown men, and even then, the boy managed

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:31.960
to send them flying through the room.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:36.400
Violent manifestations and attacks are not
uncommon, which is why exorcists often deploy

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:37.830
physical restraints.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:42.140
On one occasion, a patient succeeded in attacking
Amorth directly, delivering a kick so strong

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.660
that it broke his leg.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.280
The priest had to wear a cast for a month.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:50.090
Most attacks directed at the priest take a
different form: spitting.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:54.970
This is a manifestation of the scorn and spite
felt by demons against the exorcist and his

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:55.970
prayers.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.230
In some cases, the projectile was more than
just saliva.

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:02.020
In one particularly tough ritual, Amorth went
to cover the patient’s mouth while she was

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:03.020
foaming and spitting.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:07.000
When he retracted his hand, he found it filled
with metal nails.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:11.420
This was not surprising to Amorth: spitting
or simply producing metallic items in the

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:16.090
patient’s mouth is a common trick used by
devils to hurt and scare their victims.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:20.040
He recalled patients slowly ejecting from
their mouth large metal spikes, shards of

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:24.110
glass, or even a radio, which came out one
piece at the time.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:28.140
During his career, Father Amorth has frequently
spoken about the film The Exorcist.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:31.690
While praising it for raising awareness about
the practice of exorcism, he pointed out that

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:35.250
the ritual used was not the correct one, and
most of all that the symptoms displayed by

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.390
victim Regan were exaggerated.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.760
So, can the head spin by 180 degrees?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:39.760
Absolutely no!

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:42.050
What of people bending backwards in a bridge
position and walking like spiders?

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:47.350
Well, victims can contort in unnatural ways,
angles and shapes, but they are unlikely to

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.870
crawl like arachnids.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:49.870
How about green projectile vomiting?

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:53.270
Vomiting does happen, but never with such
force.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:54.670
And can patients levitate?

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:59.060
Well, actually Amorth confirmed that this
does happen, although he only experienced

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:00.640
it twice in thirty years.

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:04.330
On another occasion, he witnessed something
even more chilling: a possessed old lady was

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:06.700
able to walk on walls like a reptile.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:11.860
Lastly: do patients’ voices sound ‘double’,
as though there is more than one entity within?

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:14.170
That could be the most interesting one of
all.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:18.230
Amorth always maintained that Satan, or his
demons, do not like to talk.

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.520
This is because they hate being detected.

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:25.430
However, when they are discovered, they may
engage in short dialogue with the exorcist,

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:29.510
usually limited to verbal abuse or curt answers
to the priest’s questions.

00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:33.250
The entities may not reveal their name when
questioned; if they do, they often claim to

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.800
be Satan, or Beelzebub.

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.190
What they will easily reveal is how many of
them are within the host.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:42.390
Sometimes three, five, seven, perhaps even
a legion of demons.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:46.360
Even then, though, ‘double’ or ‘multiple’
sounding voices are extremely rare, but not

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:47.360
impossible...

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.870
For a full account of the battles of Father
Amorth, I can only advise that you look up

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:55.760
one of the several books he published on his
experiences, including “An Exorcist Tells

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:59.680
His Story”, “My Battle Against Satan”
or “Memoirs of an Exorcist”.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:04.460
Now, it is fair to wonder if the Exorcist-in-Chief
at the Vatican has ever felt fear during his

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.500
daily occult struggles.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:10.440
Even if one does not believe in demons, we
are still talking about confronting patients

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:15.640
who are deeply disturbed and potentially dangerous,
for several times a day.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:18.470
Journalists have asked him many times: are
you scared of Satan?

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:20.910
His reply:
“Absolutely not.

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:29.200
It is him,
who is afraid

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.200
of me.”

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.200
The Press and Father Amorth
Father Gabriele Amorth has always had an open

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:35.750
and positive relationship with the press,
an important channel to raise awareness on

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:36.750
exorcism.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:40.230
He believed that, prior to the three most
recent Popes, Vatican leadership has not done

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:42.740
enough to support exorcism in the public consciousness.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:47.520
It is perceived as an ancient and outdated
practice of the Church, rather than a noble,

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:48.990
very real fight against the Devil.

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:52.880
Amorth has never been shy about his critical
view of top Church officials.

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:57.870
He has accused them of trying to replace the
Roman Ritual of exorcisms with less powerful

00:20:57.870 --> 00:21:02.650
variations, and of trying to ban ‘diagnostic
exorcisms’, a key step in the discernment

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:03.650
process.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:07.940
In 2012, Father Amorth successfully prevented
both changes from taking effect.

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:11.540
Two years later, he scored another victory
-- receiving an official acknowledgement from

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:17.180
the Vatican for the International Association
of Exorcists, which he had co-founded in 1990.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:20.730
These conflicts with the Vatican have been
exacerbated by a series of interviews in the

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:25.820
2000s in which Father Amorth stated that the
Holy See had been infiltrated by demons, and

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:30.960
that the series of church sex scandals could
be attributed to satanic influence or downright

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:31.960
possession.

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:35.610
Amorth had partially toned down these claims
before his death, stating that Cardinals and

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:40.230
other leaders were not immune from temptations
brought forward by Satan, who was more active

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:42.630
than ever in his fight against Catholicism.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:46.680
It must be said that Amorth did not pull any
punches when it came to accusing pretty much

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:49.860
everything and everyone of being an ally of
Evil.

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:54.290
He went as far as calling yoga as a ‘satanic’
practice, as – according to him - it is

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:58.880
linked to eastern religions, which are sometimes
centered around the belief of reincarnation.

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:01.460
Perhaps his best-known target is the Harry
Potter franchise.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:04.200
In his view, the Wizarding World described
by J.K.

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:08.890
Rowling encourages children to believe in
black magic and to distance themselves from

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:10.090
Christian prayer.

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:14.370
However, instead of denting his popularity,
these controversies have contributed to Father

00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:17.540
Amorth becoming the most famous living Catholic
exorcist.

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:21.630
And so, it was only a matter of time before
he came face-to-face with the man behind the

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:24.600
most famous fictional exorcist.

00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:33.030
Last Exorcism: Session 9
In 2016, filmmaker William Friedkin, director

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:36.250
of The Exorcist, interviewed Father Amorth
for Vanity Fair.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:40.460
Friedkin took the occasion to ask permission
to join the priest in one of his exorcism

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:41.460
sessions.

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:45.890
His footage of the exorcism of a young woman
called Cristina formed the backbone of Friedkin’s

00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:49.960
latest release, the documentary “The Devil
and Father Amorth”.

00:22:49.960 --> 00:22:53.490
When Friedkin met Amorth, he had been exorcising
Cristina for nine months.

00:22:53.490 --> 00:22:58.040
It all began with another patient, a woman
in her thirties whose name has never been

00:22:58.040 --> 00:22:59.040
revealed.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:03.540
After a long depression, she was found one
day by her brother, Paolo, writhing on the

00:23:03.540 --> 00:23:06.690
floor, her twisting body shaken by convulsions.

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:10.530
According to witnesses, she would be found
howling like a wolf and crawling on walls

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:11.630
like a snake.

00:23:11.630 --> 00:23:15.210
This state continued for several days, and
a psychiatrist was not able to help.

00:23:15.210 --> 00:23:18.760
Amorth took charge, and the patient was healed
after four sessions.

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:23.120
Following the experience, Paolo became one
of Father Amorth’s most trusted assistants.

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:28.940
And it was Paolo who, years later, met Cristina
at Mass, and he noticed how she looked distressed,

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:30.560
disoriented, and disturbed.

00:23:30.560 --> 00:23:33.550
Paolo brought her case to Amorth’s attention.

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:36.790
According to Amorth, Cristina’s brother
and his girlfriend were members of a satanic

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:41.320
cult, and they may have caused Cristina’s
plight after performing an occult ritual.

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:45.110
Whatever the cause, it was clear to him that
Cristina needed his help.

00:23:45.110 --> 00:23:49.270
After following the discernment procedure,
the priest started to exorcise her in August

00:23:49.270 --> 00:23:50.650
of 2015.

00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:55.070
Friedkin was allowed to film the ninth exorcism
session in early 2016.

00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:58.070
Clips of the exorcism session are available
on Youtube, and you will find the links below.

00:23:58.070 --> 00:24:01.690
For the most part, I will leave it to you
to take your own conclusion; I will comment

00:24:01.690 --> 00:24:03.090
only on a couple of things.

00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:06.570
First, it’s remarkable just how calm and
unfazed Father Amorth appears.

00:24:06.570 --> 00:24:09.690
In one clip he thumbs his nose at the demon
inside Cristina.

00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:13.631
And, although the subtitles miss this, my
Italian researcher assures me that he tells

00:24:13.631 --> 00:24:15.670
the entity to
“Shut up!

00:24:15.670 --> 00:24:17.640
You ain’t worth a cigarette butt!”

00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:19.660
You may also notice Cristina’s behaviour.

00:24:19.660 --> 00:24:24.520
She appears to be in a trance-like state,
but she is alert and reactive to Amorth’s

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:25.520
ritual.

00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:26.520
Very reactive.

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:29.352
As she thrashes about on her chair, or sometimes
attempts to attack the priest himself, she

00:24:29.352 --> 00:24:32.060
is barely held down by two well-built men.

00:24:32.060 --> 00:24:36.770
Then, as Amorth orders the demon to leave
Cristina’s body, in Latin, the patient replies

00:24:36.770 --> 00:24:38.840
in Italian:
“NEVER!”

00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:42.070
According to Friedkin, Cristina had never
studied Latin at school.

00:24:42.070 --> 00:24:46.570
Finally, when Amorth asks how many demons
are there, Cristina’s voice turns different.

00:24:46.570 --> 00:24:50.440
She has been growling and snarling all through
the clip, but at this point, her voice sounds

00:24:50.440 --> 00:24:53.500
… ‘double’…as if many voices speak
from within.

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:55.090
She first answers
“Eighty.

00:24:55.090 --> 00:24:56.550
Eighty Leaders!”

00:24:56.550 --> 00:24:58.260
And later
“We are Armies!

00:24:58.260 --> 00:24:59.260
Armies!

00:24:59.260 --> 00:25:00.260
Armies!”

00:25:00.260 --> 00:25:02.810
Then, Amorth concludes the ritual with the
Sign of the Cross.

00:25:02.810 --> 00:25:06.750
Amorth later confided to Friedkin that this
case was particularly unsettling.

00:25:06.750 --> 00:25:10.980
During a previous session, Cristina’s entity
had recited back to Father Amorth all his

00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:12.250
past sins.

00:25:12.250 --> 00:25:16.380
This was something that only the exorcist
and his father confessor could know.

00:25:16.380 --> 00:25:20.640
Amorth and Cristina were due to meet again
to conclude the exorcism, but her family kept

00:25:20.640 --> 00:25:21.910
postponing appointments.

00:25:21.910 --> 00:25:26.100
Friedkin saw Cristina and her relatives again
in August, but was threatened with legal action

00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:27.610
if he divulged his footage.

00:25:27.610 --> 00:25:30.470
Their concern was that making it public would
spread Satan’s work.

00:25:30.470 --> 00:25:35.190
As Friedkin brushed off the threats, Cristina’s
family cut ties with both the film maker and

00:25:35.190 --> 00:25:36.190
Amorth.

00:25:36.190 --> 00:25:40.180
Unfortunately, the chief exorcist would not
have been able to complete his work with Cristina,

00:25:40.180 --> 00:25:41.390
even if he was able to.

00:25:41.390 --> 00:25:45.140
Already in poor health throughout the summer,
Father Amorth contracted pneumonia and was

00:25:45.140 --> 00:25:46.970
hospitalised at the beginning of September.

00:25:46.970 --> 00:25:53.520
At the age of 91, Father Gabriele Amorth died
from complications of pneumonia on the September

00:25:53.520 --> 00:25:54.980
16, 2016.

00:25:54.980 --> 00:25:59.220
According to his assistant, he remained alert
and jovial to the last moment, often removing

00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:10.730
his oxygen mask to blow raspberries at visiting
friends, whenever they started crying.

00:26:10.730 --> 00:26:11.900
Is any of this real?

00:26:11.900 --> 00:26:16.800
So far, I have presented possession and exorcism
from the point of view of Gabriele Amorth.

00:26:16.800 --> 00:26:21.110
Do I believe that demons and spirits can invade
and control an individual?

00:26:21.110 --> 00:26:23.690
I am not going to answer that.

00:26:23.690 --> 00:26:24.690
Sorry!

00:26:24.690 --> 00:26:30.040
What I will choose to highlight is the perspective
of medicine and psychiatry on demonic possession.

00:26:30.040 --> 00:26:33.960
For decades, since the beginning of modern
psychiatry and psychoanalysis, the official

00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:39.310
stance was that almost all possessions could
be explained as extreme cases of psychosis

00:26:39.310 --> 00:26:40.310
and schizophrenia.

00:26:40.310 --> 00:26:44.540
In recent years, the diagnosis has changed,
and the DSM 5 – the official ‘handbook’

00:26:44.540 --> 00:26:49.900
of American Psychiatry – identifies demonic
possession as a form of Dissociative Identity

00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:50.900
Disorder.

00:26:50.900 --> 00:26:55.770
These are perfectly viable explanations; however,
some psychiatrists admit that mental illness

00:26:55.770 --> 00:27:01.120
cannot explain all observed phenomena, and
that exorcism rites can be considered as a

00:27:01.120 --> 00:27:02.470
legitimate therapy.

00:27:02.470 --> 00:27:07.060
For example, The British Journal of Psychiatry
published an article on the use of antipsychotic

00:27:07.060 --> 00:27:10.740
clopenthixol to treat
“Exorcism-resistant Ghost Possession”.

00:27:10.740 --> 00:27:14.010
Which acknowledges that exorcism may be a
cure.

00:27:14.010 --> 00:27:18.590
More recently, in an interview with the Telegraph,
Psychiatry Professor Richard Gallagher, of

00:27:18.590 --> 00:27:23.380
New York Medical College and Columbia University,
stated that demonic possessions are real and

00:27:23.380 --> 00:27:26.350
that patients seeking exorcism should be taken
seriously.

00:27:26.350 --> 00:27:31.480
While I could go on forever with arguments
and counter-arguments, I will leave it to

00:27:31.480 --> 00:27:37.630
you, in the comments: is possession a psychiatric
illness, or can evil spirits haunt a human

00:27:37.630 --> 00:27:38.630
soul?

00:27:38.630 --> 00:27:39.790
Conclusion
I really do hope you enjoyed today’s video.

00:27:39.790 --> 00:27:45.430
The power of Biographics compels you to hit
that ‘like’ button, to share and subscribe.

00:27:45.430 --> 00:27:50.100
Don’t forget to head off to our Geographics
Channel if you haven’t seen yet our video

00:27:50.100 --> 00:28:06.610
on the Vatican and its many secrets.

